// Mission TT1_5, OpenTT's own map: generated.
// The Neverending Stream (tt1_5): OpenTT's own green map (a 368 m mission area), the living stream.
// Layout (x east, y north; green spawns south, blue north); point-symmetric about the island:
// the stream meanders west to east across the middle in a bed about 28 m wide, 8 m under
// the banks (walls of 24 degrees); round the island it splits into two channels;
// (0, 0)       the island: a low hill between the channels, a clearing on top (levelled),
// old trees on it and round it, a power-up by it; a waterfall (3 m) at each end of it, where
// the stream splits (x -80) and joins again (x 80); jump pads in both
// channels throw tanks up onto it; a ford from each team's bank into its
// channel (north bank at x -26, south bank at x 26);
// (-142, ~18), (142, ~-18)  the fords: ramps down both banks, the water wide and
// shallow; a reload arch at the top of the north ramp (west) and of the
// south ramp (east); rowboats pulled up on the sand;
// (-98, ~60), (98, ~-60)  the leaps: boost pads before kickers on the north bank
// (west) and the south bank (east) jump the stream;
// (62, 92), (-62, -92)  the bluffs: high ground over the stream, ramps away from it;
// the bed: the low flank route, fallen logs and boulders for cover, boost pads below the fords
// racing towards the island; power-ups in both channels, on the bluffs and in the
// bed; health on the far flanks.
// See tt_assets::data::mission.
